    "pay": "See listing",
    "paid": false,
    "hoursAgo": 21,
    "datePosted": "2026-11-20T16:08:27.000Z",
    "description": "Job Title : Coordinator, Grants, Contract and Compliance Function : Oversee grants, contracts, and compliance activities. Department : Finance, Grants and Contracts Position: 2 Reports To: Lead, Grants, Contract and Compliance Contract Term : Indefinite Duty Station : Addis Ababa with 30% travel to regional towns and project implementation sites. Who are we? We’re Population Services International (PSI), the world’s leading non‐profit social marketing organization. We work to make it easier for people in the developing world to lead healthier lives and plan the families they desire by marketing affordable products and services that range from mosquito nets to contraceptives to HIV testing. We are a $560m enterprise based in Washington, DC, operating in the private and public sectors in more than 65 countries. There are over 9,000 “PSI’ers” around the world. It’s a diverse group of entrepreneurs and professionals with an unusually wide range of backgrounds - from the medical industry to the music business - all with unique skills we bring to the job. Purpose of the Job! To coordinate and oversee the effective implementation of grants, contracts, and subaward management processes, ensuring that subrecipients comply with applicable donor requirements, PSI terms and conditions, contractual obligations, and relevant regulatory frameworks. The position is responsible for coordinating subrecipient due diligence, risk assessments, subaward and subcontract management, subaward performance monitoring, compliance reviews, and partner capacity-strengthening initiatives. The role also timely review subrecipients financial reporting, disbursement, audit readiness, and the identification and mitigation of compliance risks across the assigned portfolios, in collaboration with relevant internal teams and under the guidance of the Grants, Contracts and Compliance Lead. Sounds like you? Read on! Main Duties and Responsibilities: Key Result Areas: Subaward due diligence and risk assessment process. Sub-grantee monitoring and performance management (eg., number of monitoring visits, sub awards actual Vs forecast performance) Contract award and implementation. Capacity building (eg., active use of capacity building plan; sub awards capacity building on financial management and internal control systems) Compliance management (eg., compliance within portfolio, deviations from standards, actions against deviations, sub awards) Main Duties and Responsibilities: Maintain, manage and monitor a grants management system to ensure proper subaward management. Conduct pre-award assessments of grantees in coordination with other staff, develop capacity building plans, and provide support to grantees to address any gaps identified. Participate in grantee’s work plan and budget review process. Work closely with grantees to strengthen their capacity and follow up on site visits and capacity building action plans. Develop mechanisms for appropriate monitoring and financial management to fulfill different donors’ requirements for grantees. Develop the periodic monitoring plan as per the grantees program and financial performance. Monitor and evaluate the performance of grantees, including regular site visits with project staff. Ensure financial accountability for sub-grants, including the review of invoices and financial reports and documentation submitted by grantees. For cost-reimbursable subawards, conduct a risk-based sampling of transactions and verify supporting documentation, complete invoice testing form, financial checklist, and management letter tools to document approved, questioned, and disallowed costs, and summarize internal control weaknesses and action items, as applicable, and ensure timely posting of subaward advances, liquidations, and reimbursements. For fixed amount subawards, ensure thorough verification of deliverable achievement and prompt payment. Ensure that all subrecipients meet funder/donor and PSI requirements, including regarding compliance, financial management, and reporting. Participate in Coordination and monitor development of grant management and sub-award trainings for PSI/Ethiopia operations (eg., finance, operations) and program staff on the use of SR management tools. Ensure that the sub awardee complies with donor requirements, internal policies, local laws, and international regulations while maintaining accountability and minimizing risks. Oversee report review for compliance with terms and conditions, donor and PSI rules and regulations, provide feedback to grantees, coordinating the timely cash disbursements of Sub Recipients. Verify that subaward activities are implemented according to approved project documents and budgets. Organize periodic financial review packages and ensure proper documentation. Provide technical support on grants contract and compliance management for staff and subgrantees. Review periodic advance requests and financial expenditure reports, journalize and post data on QBE. Ensure grantees proper documentation and filing to be ready for internal and external audit, including verification of complete and compliant subaward files Follow up on grantees budget utilization status. Monitor subrecipients to adherence of donor compliance, grant agreements, organizational policies and PSI terms and conditions. Support the Grants, Contracts and Compliance Lead on grants, contracts, and compliance management, administrative activities. Review grantees annual and periodic budget review and modification requests. Facilitate training and orientation for grantees and organization staff on donor regulations, procurement procedures, safeguarding, anti-fraud measures, and ethics policies. Participate in the project’s subaward closeout process. Coordinate audit engagements and provide required documentation for internal and external audits. Provide any other administrative support related to Grants contract and compliance management activities as needed.",
