    "description": "Job Title: Data Clerk and Receptionist Reports to: Clinic Head and MEL advisor Job Location: Addis Ababa Contract Details: Indefinite, subject to budget availability Salary: As per the organizational salary scale. Who are we? We’re Population Services International (PSI), the world’s leading non‐profit social marketing organization. We work to make it easier for people in the developing world to lead healthier lives and plan the families they desire by marketing affordable products and services that range from mosquito nets to contraceptives to HIV testing. We are a $560m enterprise based in Washington, DC, operating in the private and public sectors in more than 65 countries. There are over 9,000 “PSI’ers” around the world. It’s a diverse group of entrepreneurs and professionals with an unusually wide range of backgrounds - from the medical industry to the music business - all with unique skills we bring to the job. Purpose of the Job! The Data Clerk / Receptionist maintains accurate and up-to-date data records for the organization, serves as the first point of contact for clients and visitors, and manages daily cash collection, reconciliation, and timely submission to the Finance team. The role uses computer devices and software to enter, verify, and update data; works closely with M&E, clinic, and program staff to ensure data quality; and supports donor reporting and data-driven decision making. Sounds like you? Read on! Main Duties and Responsibilities: Data Management Create and maintain spreadsheets to track important customer information and orders. Transfer data from hard copy to digital databases and input text-based and numerical information from source documents accurately and efficiently. Update customer information in databases and organize existing data in spreadsheets. Verify outdated data, review data for deficiencies or errors, and make necessary corrections to records. Search for and retrieve information contained in files. Perform regular database backups to secure data, ensuring it is protected from loss and corruption and easily accessible when needed. Sort and file hard copies of paperwork after electronic data entry. Support data analysis and presentation with new and explanatory approaches. Work with M&E and program staff to compile ongoing M&E data in a way that responds to donor requests. Support project staff in programming data collection tools for monitoring and other periodic surveys required by the organization and respective donors. Identify the indicator-based information needs of the organization and donors, and design databases and data analysis templates that strengthen data-driven decision making. Assist with special projects requiring large volumes of data entry and provide ad-hoc data entry support across departments Reception and Front Desk Welcome and register clients, visitors, and guests, and direct them to the appropriate staff or service points. Answer, screen, and route incoming calls; take accurate messages and follow up as needed. Receive, sort, and distribute incoming mail, packages, and documents; maintain a log of correspondence. Maintain a clean, organized, and professional reception area. Operate common office equipment such as scanners, printers, and photocopiers. Provide occasional administrative support, including scheduling appointments and meeting rooms. Cash Collection, Reconciliation and Submission to Finance Collect cash payments (e.g., service fees) from clients and issue official receipts for every transaction. Record all cash collected daily in the cash collection log or system. Reconcile daily cash collections against receipts and records, and promptly report any discrepancies to the supervisor. Safeguard cash on hand in line with organizational financial policies and internal controls. Prepare and submit cash collection reports, together with the reconciled cash and supporting documents, to the Finance team on a timely basis. Obtain acknowledgment of cash handed over to Finance and keep copies of all supporting records for audit purposes.",
