    "datePosted": "2026-11-20T15:35:04.000Z",
    "description": "Department: Economic Empowerment Reporting To: Economic Empowerment and WASH Director Required Number of position - One Duty Station: Head Office/Addis Ababa Remuneration: As per the organization pay scale plus other PSI/Ethiopia staff benefits Who we are? We’re Population Services International (PSI), the world’s leading non‐profit social marketing organization. We work to make it easier for people in the developing world to lead healthier lives and plan the families they desire by marketing affordable products and services that range from mosquito nets to contraceptives to HIV testing. We are a $560m enterprise based in Washington, DC, operating in the private and public sectors in more than 65 countries. Join us! There are over 9,000 “PSI’ers” around the world. It’s a diverse group of entrepreneurs and professionals with an unusually wide range of backgrounds - from the medical industry to the music business - all with unique skills we bring to the job. PSI/Ethiopia wants to reimagine healthcare, put the consumer at the center, and whenever possible, bring quality care to the front door. We achieve health impact in Ethiopia by working with both government and private partners and harvesting technology innovation to bring quality care closer to communities, schools, and homes. We empower consumers by including them in the design of healthcare solutions, offering them more healthcare choices, and helping them to have a voice in influencing national priorities. We work with all market actors in the health system to understand their needs, designing and delivering solutions so that market systems can sustainably serve consumers for the long term, helping to support the Government of Ethiopia in achieving Universal Health Coverage. We are looking for a dynamic and experienced Project Manager to ensure the efficient, timely, and high-quality implementation of the nutrition market system Project at PSI/E from inception to completion. The role involves establishing strong partnerships with government entities, implementing partners, consortium partners, private sector actors, and traditional market stakeholders; overseeing planning, monitoring, and reporting of the project implementation and impact; leading project initiatives and conducting regular team reviews; supporting fundraising efforts; and coordinating both internal and external communications and project partnerships. This position at PSI/Ethiopia will be part of the extended leadership team that focuses on supporting market-based innovations that increase the consumption of fruits and vegetables in Ethiopia especially by strengthening traditional markets and creating demand for healthy diets through consumer insights, human-centered design, social and behavior change, and market-based demand-generation interventions. Key responsibilities In close consultation with the Economic Empowerment and WASH Director, oversea the project implementation, work plans, budgets, performance tracking systems, ensuring timely delivery of project milestones, efficient resource utilization, compliance with donor requirements, and achievement of project targets. Lead the design, procurement, implementation, and quality assurance of consumer and market research activities, including behavioral assessments, consumer segmentation studies, vendor assessments, retail audits, and market system analyses, ensuring findings are translated into actionable consumer insights, intervention design, and practical market-based solutions. Coordinate and manage human-centered design and co-creation processes with consumers, vendors, retailers, private sector actors, and government stakeholders to identify market constraints, generate solutions, conduct rapid prototyping, and refine interventions based on user feedback and evidence, actionable consumer insights, intervention design, and practical market-based solutions. Oversee PSI's technical contribution to the development and implementation of demand generation and behavior change campaigns, including branding, merchandising, consumer promotions, retail activation events, digital engagement initiatives, and community outreach activities aimed at increasing fruit and vegetable consumption among target populations, in close coordination with key consortium partners Manage partnerships with vendors, retailers, aggregators, market actors, and private sector organizations to improve product availability, affordability, visibility, and customer experience while strengthening the responsiveness of local food markets, including vendor-mediated promotion, pricing and incentive mechanisms, and improved point-of-purchase experiences. Closely work with the M&E team on the monitoring, evaluation, and learning activities, including reviewing the project performance data, assessing intervention effectiveness, documenting lessons learned, and making evidence-based adjustments to improve project outcomes and maximize impact, while supporting structured learning cycles and evidence generation in collaboration with consortium research partners. Produce and disseminate technical reports, case studies, learning briefs, and scale-up recommendations to support stakeholder decision-making, promote adoption of successful models, strengthen private sector engagement, and facilitate the adoption, sustainability and wider replication of effective market-based approaches. Provide technical assistance and support to program research, strategic planning, and knowledge management with relevant departments/ teams. Support the development, implementation and review of relevant project related procedures and ensure compliance with donor and organization policies. Support the integration of gender, safeguarding, food safety, and inclusion priorities in collaboration with relevant technical advisors and consortium partners, particularly in activities involving women consumers, caregivers, and vendors. Contribute to business development by supporting donor mapping, concept notes and proposal development for new programs, particularly in nutrition, economic empowerment, and market systems development.",
