    "description": "Position Field Coordinator Duty station Project sourcing areas and field locations; extensive regional travel Reports to Project Manager; operational collaboration with Project Officer Employment Full-time, fixed-term project appointment Works with Agronomists, extension agents, cooperatives, farmer groups, youth enterprises and MEL 1.Project context Theday Agro Industry PLC is preparing to implement an inclusive fruit value-chain development project under the Mastercard Foundation Fund for Resilience and Prosperity (FRP). The project will strengthen direct sourcing from smallholder farmers, improve Good Agricultural Practices and post-harvest handling, support EU Organic certification readiness, expand regional distribution through youth-led enterprises, and develop local and export markets for value-added fruit products. It prioritizes dignified work and income opportunities for young women and men, including persons with disabilities and displaced young people. All activities and results will follow the final approved FRP work plan, budget and MEL framework. 2.Purpose of the position Coordinate implementation and follow-up at farm and community levels to ensure effective farmer engagement, agricultural extension, inclusive enterprise activities and market-sourcing linkages. 3.Key duties and responsibilities Coordinate field implementation plans across target sourcing areas, assigning site schedules and following up with agronomists, extension agents and mobilizers. Support transparent farmer identification, registration and onboarding, ensuring farmers understand participation and market-linkage arrangements. Coordinate farmer GAP training, practical demonstrations, post-harvest handling, climate-resilient practices and follow-up visits. Work with technical leads on fruit quality, aggregation, collection-center arrangements, supply schedules and traceability documents. Support identification and coordination of youth enterprises in seedling services, waste management, extension services and related value-chain activities where approved. Facilitate local government, farmer cooperative, TVET and community relationships and promptly escalate bottlenecks or disputes. Coordinate safe and inclusive participation of women, youth, persons with disabilities and displaced people, including feedback and referral mechanisms. Supervise completeness of training lists, visit logs, farmer supply records, service support and field documentation, submitting originals to MEL on time. Report on delivery progress, seasonal risks, farmer uptake, post-harvest challenges and action requirements; support spot checks and field verification. 4.Deliverables / performance expectations Regional and monthly field implementation schedules Verified field activity, attendance, sourcing and visit documentation Periodic field progress and issue reports Documented extension, farmer engagement and enterprise follow-up",
