    "description": "Position Local and Export Marketing Officer Duty station Addis Ababa, with market and buyer travel as needed Reports to Sales and Marketing Lead / Chief Marketing Officer; project coordination with Project Manager Employment Full-time, fixed-term or assigned project role as approved Works with Sales, QA, Production, Finance, youth distributors and Business Development 1.Project context Theday Agro Industry PLC is preparing to implement an inclusive fruit value-chain development project under the Mastercard Foundation Fund for Resilience and Prosperity (FRP). The project will strengthen direct sourcing from smallholder farmers, improve Good Agricultural Practices and post-harvest handling, support EU Organic certification readiness, expand regional distribution through youth-led enterprises, and develop local and export markets for value-added fruit products. It prioritizes dignified work and income opportunities for young women and men, including persons with disabilities and displaced young people. All activities and results will follow the final approved FRP work plan, budget and MEL framework. 2.Purpose of the position Develop and implement local and export marketing activities for Theday’s value-added fruit products, generating qualified buyer opportunities and commercially viable youth-led distribution channels. 3.Key duties and responsibilities Conduct market and buyer research for local retail, B2B ingredients, institutional channels, regional Ethiopian markets and priority export destinations. Prepare product positioning, launch plans, promotional calendars, customer segments and sales leads for jams, dried fruit and other approved product categories. Support commercial onboarding and capacity development of youth-led regional distributor SMEs, including merchandising, product knowledge and follow-up. Maintain buyer pipeline records and coordinate samples, quotations, technical inquiries, product specifications and negotiations with appropriate decision-makers. Work with QA and Production to verify factual product claims, packaging, regulatory documentation, traceability and export-readiness requirements. Coordinate trade events, digital campaigns, tastings, market visits and institutional buyer outreach within approved budgets and donor visibility rules. Collect customer feedback, competitive prices and sales-channel data to improve product mix and market entry decisions. Monitor sales and distribution activity, distributor performance and market-access outcomes; submit supporting evidence to MEL. Prepare periodic market progress reports and support viable distributor business models beyond the project period. 4.Deliverables / performance expectations Approved local and export marketing and promotion calendar Documented buyer pipeline, product inquiries and follow-up records Youth distributor onboarding and sales-support records Periodic market intelligence and commercial performance summaries",
