    "datePosted": "2026-11-20T12:19:47.000Z",
    "description": "BACKGROUND EthioChicken is a leading distributor of chickens to rural farmers in Ethiopia. We are a rapidly growing Company that believes in investing in our employees and offers them opportunities for career advancement. EthioChicken is an Ethiopian based company. Our Vision Our vision is to provide one chicken per person per year through smallholder farmers. Our Purpose Our purpose is making farmers of Ethiopia healthier and wealthier. Job Summary The Route Planning Officer is responsible for coordinating, monitoring, and documenting the timely dispatch of orders from the hatchery to designated sites. The role ensures that activities are conducted according to approved standard operating procedures, vehicle capacity, route plans, delivery priorities, and operational requirements. The position also manages rerouting activities, maintains accurate dispatch records, coordinates with the fleet and site teams, and supports the weekly reconciliation of dispatched and rerouted orders with the Finance Department. PERFORMANCE INDICATORS Early Dispatch- Ensure dispatch is started within 30 minutes after hatchery codes are released Data Handling – Ensure all dispatch and reroute-related data is kept and is ready for weekly reconciliation with finance KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Ensure that dispatch operations commence within 30 minutes after hatchery codes are released. Delays must be identified promptly, communicated to the relevant teams, and escalated to the Route Planning Supervisor when necessary. Ensure that all dispatch- and reroute-related information is accurately recorded, updated, and maintained. Records must be complete and readily available for Weekly reconciliation with the Finance Department. Ensure that all dispatch, vehicle assignment, rerouting, approval, and documentation activities are completed in accordance with approved SOPs. Ensure that cancelled or modified deliveries are rerouted and dispatched immediately to minimize operational delays and service interruptions. Ensure that vehicles are assigned according to availability, capacity, route requirements, and dispatch priorities. Ensure that dispatch-related challenges, delays, route changes, vehicle shortages, and other operational concerns are communicated promptly to the appropriate teams and managers. Start the dispatch process within 30 minutes after hatchery codes are released. Review released codes and confirm that all required dispatch information is available. Prioritize dispatches according to operational urgency, delivery requirements, route plans, and site needs. Ensure that dispatched Delivery Orders are updated and communicated to the site team. Confirm that dispatch activities are completed accurately and on time. Ensure that all dispatch activities comply with approved SOPs Reroute every cancelled delivery or Delivery Order as soon as the cancellation is confirmed. Ensure that rerouted orders are dispatched immediately. Record all rerouting information accurately, including the reason for rerouting, original route, revised route, vehicle details, timing, and responsible personnel. Coordinate with the Fleet Team regarding route modifications, vehicle changes, and revised delivery schedules. Ensure that all route and schedule changes are communicated to the affected teams. Update dispatched Delivery Orders and rerouting records in the relevant systems or trackers. Communicate any inconvenience, delay, shortage, system issue, or operational challenge related to dispatching. Initiate manual dispatch approval requests when system-based dispatch cannot be completed. Maintain clear and professional communication during urgent or high-pressure situations. EXPECTED WORKING BEHAVIOURS Start work promptly and respond quickly to dispatch requirements. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records. Communicate delays and challenges immediately. Follow approved procedures consistently. Demonstrate ownership of assigned Delivery Orders. Work collaboratively with internal teams. Remain calm and professional during urgent operational situations. Continuously look for ways to improve the dispatch process. EXPECTED REPORTS Weekly reroute summary – Every Monday Logistcs-Finanace Reconciliation- Weekly Daily undispached volume, if any List of DOs dispatched manually - daily Other upon request",
